Declares a typed test for a created body and close request.

The graph validator joins each role Use to its exact driver input/source;
this record does not prove predicate behavior or purity.

A narrow owner-frame reference relinquishment stage, never a free proof.

Fixed FrameRules allow callbacks/unknown effects and possible noncompletion;
repeated real attempts are not rejected merely for sharing an owner.

Current must-fact with possible static source explanations.

Multiple declarations on one source operation can describe different edges;
their presence here does not mean they all occurred on the current path.

An auditable action selected for one candidate.

``action`` is deliberately small and stable:

* ``TRANSFORM``: legality and cost were accepted and a backend is present;
* ``REJECT``: the opportunity is understood but cost or backend selection
  rules reject it;
* ``UNKNOWN``: evidence may support a transformation, but legality or
  cost is incomplete;
* ``KEEP``: the candidate does not apply to the observed execution.
